hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15628","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Hisham al-Dastuway, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Yaish ibn Tikhfah ibn Qays al-Ghifari, he said: My father was among the people of the Suffah, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, gave an order concerning them, and a man began to return with a man, and a man with two men, until I remained fifth of five. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Go. So we went with him to the house of Aishah, and he said: O Aishah, feed us. So she brought some greens and we ate, then she brought some hays like a sandgrouse and we ate, then he said: O Aishah, give us drink. So she brought a large cup and we drank, then she brought a small cup in which was milk and we drank. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: If you wish, spend the night, and if you wish, go to the mosque. So I said: No, rather we will go to the mosque. He said: While I was in the pre-dawn lying on my stomach, a man moved me with his foot and said: Indeed this is a lying that Allah, Blessed and Exalted, hates. So I looked, and it was the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"15629","Hashim narrated to us, Abu Muawiyah, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, from Abi Salamah, he said: Yaish ibn Tikhfah ibn Qays informed me, from his father, and his father was among the people of the Suffah, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O So-and-so, go with this with you, then he mentioned its meaning."
"15630","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Zuhayr, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Halhalah, from Nuaym ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Tikhfah al-Ghifari, he said: My father informed me that he was a guest of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with a group. He said: So we spent the night with him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out at night inspecting, and saw him lying flat on his face, so he kicked him with his foot and woke him, and said: This is the lying of the people of the Fire."
